@startuml counterfactual_architecture
title Counter-Factual Replay Architecture\n(Exact Regret Computation via Checkpoint-and-Branch)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "Original Experiment Run" {
    [Game Engine] as GE
    [Agent Bridge\n(gadget)] as AB
    [LLM Agent] as LLM
    [Decision Log\n(JSONL)] as LOG
    database "Checkpoints\n(saves)" as SAVES
}

package "Branch Replay" {
    [Game Engine\n(loaded from save)] as GE2
    [Agent Bridge\n(alternative action)] as AB2
    [Branch\nOrchestrator] as BO
    [Branch Result\n(JSONL)] as BLOG
}

package "Analysis" {
    [Regret\nCalculator] as RC
    [Paper\nFigures] as FIG
}

GE --> AB : state every 60s
AB --> LLM : query
LLM --> AB : action
AB --> GE : execute
AB --> LOG : log decision
AB --> SAVES : **SaveGame()**\nat each decision

SAVES --> GE2 : LoadGame\n(from decision N)
BO --> AB2 : inject\nalternative action
AB2 --> GE2 : execute different action
GE2 --> BLOG : log branch result

LOG --> RC
BLOG --> RC
RC --> FIG : exact regret =\n|branch_coverage - original_coverage|

note right of SAVES
  **Per checkpoint:**
  • Size: 5-20 MB
  • Save time: <1s
  • 30 saves per episode
  • ~300 MB total
end note

note right of GE2
  **Branch replay:**
  • Load time: 30-60s
  • Run time: remaining game
  • Deterministic from save
end note

@enduml


@startuml counterfactual_sequence
title Counter-Factual Replay Sequence\n(Single Branch from Decision Point)

participant "Original Run" as Orig
participant "Checkpoint\nStorage" as Save
participant "Branch Runner\n(script)" as Runner
participant "Game Engine\n(branch)" as Branch
participant "Alternative\nAgent" as Alt
participant "Regret\nAnalysis" as Regret

== Phase 1: Original Run (already completed) ==

Orig -> Save: SaveGame("d05.sav")\nat decision #5
note right of Save: State includes:\n• All unit positions\n• All RulesParams\n• Economy state\n• Map features

Orig -> Orig: Continue with\noriginal action A\n→ final coverage = 38%

== Phase 2: Identify Interesting Decision ==

Regret -> Regret: Heuristic scan:\n"Decision #5 has highest\nestimated regret (9.3%)"

== Phase 3: Branch Replay ==

Runner -> Branch: Launch engine with\n--savegame d05.sav
activate Branch

Branch -> Branch: Load state\n(30-60s startup)

Branch -> Alt: State at decision #5\n(same as original)

note right of Alt
  Alternative action B:
  "place_bs|macro_cell|7000|9500"
  (instead of original noop)
end note

Alt -> Branch: Action B

Branch -> Branch: Execute action B\n+ continue with same\nagent for D6-D29

Branch -> Branch: Run to completion\n(~20 min remaining)

Branch --> Runner: Final coverage = 52%
deactivate Branch

== Phase 4: Exact Regret ==

Runner -> Regret: Branch result: 52%
Regret -> Regret: **Exact regret =**\n**52% - 38% = 14%**\n\n(vs heuristic estimate: 9.3%)

note over Regret
  Validates heuristic accuracy:
  • Heuristic said 9.3%
  • Exact says 14%
  • Heuristic is conservative
    (underestimates true regret)
end note

@enduml


@startuml counterfactual_workflow
title Practical Workflow: When to Use Heuristic vs Exact Replay

skinparam activityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF8E1
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #E3F2FD

start

:Run full experiment\n(N=10 episodes, 29 decisions each);

:Compute heuristic regret\nfor ALL 290 decisions\n(takes: 2 seconds);

if (Any decision with\nregret > 10%?) then (yes)
    :Identify top-3 highest\nregret decisions;
    
    :Load checkpoint for\neach interesting decision;
    
    :Run 3 branch replays\n(takes: ~1 hour total);
    
    :Compute exact regret;
    
    :Report both:\n• Heuristic (all decisions)\n• Exact (top-3 validated);
else (no)
    :Report heuristic only\n(all regrets < 10%\nmeaning good planning);
endif

:Generate paper figures;

stop

note right
  **Cost comparison:**
  • Heuristic: 290 decisions in 2s
  • Exact: 3 replays × 20min = 1h
  • Ratio: 1800x faster for batch
  • Exact used only for validation
end note

@enduml
